{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1498329437,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMxMDg1NzY2MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1616#issuecomment-310857661"},"message":"Triples would also solve this. In general such task is not very rewarding. It is an attempt to bring order to a world that doesnt want to be structured.\n\nI think our search should try to make this a non issue for consumers, without having to hand tweak each dataset.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1500045842,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMxNTM4ODEzOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1616#issuecomment-315388139"},"message":"FTR: in #1630 we push users towards unified metadata keys, but there is complete freedom for tags/keywords. At the same time the new `search` is pretty powerful, so we likely don't care.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507447251,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNDk4ODMwNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1616#issuecomment-334988307"},"message":"3 months in no great ideas have emerged. With the new parser in #1630 the complexity of the situation goes up, if anything. I think focusing on the beautification of the stored data is a futile exercise -- unless constrained to a very specific domain of use case. But if the data source we are pulling from is a complicated mess, we would have to spend a disproportionate amount of energy to fix things. I am confident that are new search implementation is more adequate to deal with messy data.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507447251,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTI4MzA5OTU3Nw=="},"status":2}]}